k opportunity.  \n4. **Castling K-side K: e1-g1** – Safeguards king and activates rook, but misses tactical chance.  \n\nReason: The knight fork on c8 is the most forcing and wins material immediately. Black's bishop on c8 is undefended, and after Nxc8, Black must recapture with rook (Rxc8), losing the bishop. If Black tries to move the rook first, then I take bishop. Either way, White gains a piece (bishop for free). This improves material advantage significantly. Castling can wait a move.  \n\nAnswer: N: b6-c8"}
